# Reliability Pack

Use when work changes state, resources, partial success, or recovery from failures.

- Identify relevant failure conditions and what remains committed or changed after a partial failure.
- Consider cancellation, time limits, cleanup, repeated execution, and resource ownership where they apply.
- Retry only when the operation's side effects make it safe; use the project's actual constraints rather than invented retry policies.
- Make failure and recovery observable without exposing sensitive data or changing an established error contract silently.
- Verify a representative failure/recovery path proportionally to the risk. Label untested failure scenarios as hypotheses.
